{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.771,
   "text": "You just got hired at twenty dollars an hour, you worked eighty hours, and your first paycheck should be sixteen hundred dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 6.87,
   "end": 10.268,
   "text": "Then you open it, and it says about thirteen hundred sixty-nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 10.417,
   "end": 13.608,
   "text": "Wait, who took two hundred thirty dollars from my check?"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 13.757,
   "end": 20.035,
   "text": "Picture your paycheck as a sixteen hundred dollar pizza, and three people grab a slice before you get a single bite."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 20.135,
   "end": 24.492,
   "text": "Social Security takes six point two percent, ninety-nine dollars and twenty cents."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 24.592,
   "end": 29.235,
   "text": "Medicare grabs one point four five percent, another twenty-three dollars and twenty cents."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 29.335,
   "end": 35.405,
   "text": "Then federal income tax takes about one hundred eight dollars, and in most states, your state grabs a slice too."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 35.803,
   "end": 44.208,
   "text": "So it feels like you just got robbed, but those first two slices are how you earn the right to collect Social Security and Medicare when you're older."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 44.307,
   "end": 50.741,
   "text": "The tax slice is only an estimate, and if too much gets taken, you get the difference back as a refund."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 51.078,
   "end": 59.431,
   "text": "And here's the part nobody tells you, because your boss pays another one hundred twenty-two dollars and forty cents on top, a matching slice you never even see."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 59.828,
   "end": 64.446,
   "text": "You thought your pizza got smaller, but it was actually bigger than you ever saw."
  }
 ],
